@startuml Maintenance Board Participant Diagram
title Figure X: Maintenance Board Initialization & Data Flow Participant Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

actor "Maintenance Staff" as User
participant "MaintenanceScheduler" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "MaintenanceFilters" as Filters <<Component>>
participant "MaintenanceStats" as StatsDisplay <<Component>>
participant "SupabaseService" as Service <<Control>>
database "Supabase DB" as DB <<Database>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Navigate to Maintenance Page
activate UI

== Data Fetching & Status Refresh ==
UI -> Service : refreshTaskStatuses()
activate Service
Service -> DB : SELECT * FROM maintenance_tasks
activate DB
DB --> Service : tasks
deactivate DB
Service -> DB : UPDATE status for overdue/pending tasks
Service --> UI : Array of current tasks
deactivate Service

UI -> Service : getYearlyStats(currentYear)
activate Service
Service -> DB : SELECT * FROM maintenance_stats
activate DB
DB --> Service : stats
deactivate DB
Service --> UI : stats
deactivate Service

UI -> StatsDisplay : Update KPI Cards (Completion %, Overdue Count)

== User Interaction (Filtering) ==
User -> Filters : Input Search or Category Filter
activate Filters
Filters -> UI : onSearchChange() / onCategoryChange()
deactivate Filters

UI -> UI : filteredTasks = tasks.filter(...)
UI -> UI : Render TaskItem components

note right of UI
  **Local Filtering:**
  The board filters and sorts
  data client-side for near-
  instant UI responsiveness.
end note

@enduml
